      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.3, & \\,x=3 \\\\ 0.7, & \\,x=5 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ is shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=2] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 0.3+5\\cdot 0.7 \\\\  & =4.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
